  "absent": "Count all missing roots caused by early termination.",
  "choice_inputs": "Own pre-action seat-visible observation, own v1 action, previous public rosters only. No seed, opponent actions or hidden carbon. Unknown carbon=0. This is not calibrated expected value.",
  "budget": "Up to three operators: two highest-cargo >=1 collectors in range of an owned bank in remaining H<=2; one collector <=35 that can land outside both sides' bases on a current shortest route of a hostile collector with cargo>=100 within 2 of its home. If no independent blocker, permit third returner. Candidates original or feasible bank-decreasing routes and wait if time, once for each selected worker. Do not introduce new friendly nonbank collisions or change recruiters/other orders; own bank exception permitted.",
  "scenarios": "Three fixed reactive projections: fastest own bank in compass order; reverse compass with prior heading as tie-break; tactical light intercept else home, with optional visible harvest given slack. Empty workers and planters may repeat their last move, else step deterministically. Bases idle during continuation. First opponent orders shared, final orders adapt to the simulated child state for both teams.",
  "scoring": "Evaluate full terminal cash difference of both parties from visible-world FastCarbon; veto any extinct projected branch. Require minimum predicted gain>0.01 and mean>=5 across 3 situations. Prefer highest mean then fewer changes, deterministic order.",
  "evaluation": "Full official replay from taped simultaneous actions for every source. H1 exact with unchanged actual simultaneous opponent order. H2 exact first transition with actual simultaneous opponent order. Follow each resulting state with three public and reactive proxies for BOTH sides; publish separately from actual Master strength. Include both sides, counterexamples, move/foregone proceeds, time and source terminal scores.",
  "criteria": "For queue-specific support require realized evaluation edits where >=2 own workers intend to post at the same home and positive average exact/conditional margin there. No new native games or claim of improved win rate. Distinguish shared-home, return and intercept. Do not refit on this split."
